  "final_text": "The dashboard and the alert rule both exist. I didn't open the dashboard to check how the panels render, and I haven't seen the rule fire.\n\n**Data:** The data view's time field is `timestamp`. The main fields are `response` (a string, so 5xx is matched through `response.keyword`), `bytes`, `extension`, `clientip`, `geo.src`, `geo.dest`, `machine.os`, `host`, `url` and `request`.\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-60995af8 Web logs overview\" has 4 panels and defaults to the last 7 days. It's at http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-60995af8-web-logs-overview-b344b6ca9d1a\n- Total requests (single-number metric)\n- Requests over time (line chart)\n- Requests by response code (pie chart)\n- Average bytes by extension (bar chart)\n\n**Rule:** \"EFF-60995af8 5xx spike\" (id `53e822c8-f716-4a0e-8599-49d56d58a1dc`) is an Elasticsearch query rule. It runs every minute and fires when more than 10 documents with `response.keyword` matching `5*` appear in a 5-minute window. The tool created it disabled, so I enabled it. It has no action connector, so a firing will show up in Kibana but won't notify anyone.",
